WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
Imagine a study of 20 countries.

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.300
For each one, plot how much
saturated fat people eat,

3
00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:08.890
against the death rate from heart disease.

4
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.130
The dots climb together.

5
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:15.290
Say the correlation
coefficient comes out at 0.85.

6
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.250
A coefficient runs from minus 1 to plus 1,

7
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.270
so that looks like a close link.

8
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.540
Fat in, heart disease up.

9
00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:23.700
Case closed?

10
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.470
Does that prove the fat is the cause?

11
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:31.090
In this mission, you'll learn to read
correlation coefficients from scatter plots.

12
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:36.200
Then you'll weigh up what it takes to
show that one thing really causes another.

13
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:41.280
Your mission: decide whether more fat
and more heart disease prove that the fat

14
00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:42.270
is the cause.
